one last job I can do it who's the mark  the one responsible for it all the cults  the black magic this mark on my hand  we're gonna kill the black eye bastard  himself what you want to kill the  outsider you want to kill God tying up  loose ends in a series focus on  political intrigue and all things  metaphysical can't be easy and  dishonored death of the outsider a  standalone game capping off the story  from dishonour - it covers the exploits  of various sight characters on a more  personal quest that doesn't overstay its  welcome Arkane Studios continues its  tradition of coming up with an  incredibly inventive and cunning game  about elusive assassins making their  mark on the world around them while  choosing where and when to make the  tough choices my name is billy lurk  though there aren't many people who  remember for years i stayed hidden  captain of a ship called the dreadful  whale set several months after dishonor  to emily kaldwin and Corvo attano has  since left the Isle of carnico leaving  Billy lurk under the alias Megan foster  in dishonor - to return to her old ways  to track down her former mentor doubt  pulling from her skills working under  the master assassin they form a plan to  confront the outsider a deity of the  void roam an instigator of events  throughout the series Billy lurk will  use her newfound powers to sneak loot  and track down key targets to find a way  to eliminate the demigod once and for  all with no mark bestowed from the  outsider she is freed from the demigods  watchful gaze making the chaos system of  past games non-existent this serves to  set the tone for what players can expect  in death of the outsider where the moral  ambiguity of the story matches the  gameplay allowing her to go about  missions in different and inventive ways  often going for a more improvised style  that blends lethal and non-lethal moves  much like the previous games death of  the outsider makes effective use of  large open levels with each city block  holding a number of side events and  points of interest Billie's approach is  a bit different compared to the exploits  of Corvo Emily and doubt focusing more  on seeking justice for all that's  happened in her past her story aims to  round out the narrative presented in  both sonnet games but the general flow  feels lacking and somewhat unearned  while starting strong the story  eventually runs out of steam with its  final missions falling a bit flat with  that said there are many details packed  in for dishonored fans revealing  important notes that flesh out the  events since the last game every night  for weeks the same terrifying dream a  street fight my arm dead and lying in  the gutter my eye gouge doubt by a grand  guard sword but when I wake up they  still heard for hours gives me the  creeps  as an immersive sim each character and  object in the game space can be  manipulated opening up some rather  interesting gameplay opportunities like  baiting enemies with thrown bottles to  walk into traps for some rather creative  options like using the semblance power  to mimic the appearance of other  characters to get the jump on targets  the AI and dishonored is as sharp as  ever and will require some planning to  get through unscathed but if going in  full force is your thing then the game  won't discourage you with the more lacks  gameplay systems on display there's much  more incentive to experiment with the  tools at your disposal though Billy's  overall repertoire of skills are much  more lean compared to the other  characters while core row and Emily had  a sizable pool of powers the lone  assassin has just three along with the  side ability to wrap whisper where she  can hear the thoughts of nearby rodents  to learn clues and tidbits about  characters in the area focusing on the  key areas of traversal recon and  subterfuge her powers will cover the key  areas of what players will need  throughout their missions one power in  particular named foresight allows Billy  to project yourself as a specter to  scout and mark targets this skill is a  standout proving its usefulness time and  again when locating bone charms and key  items while the core gameplay systems  are razor-sharp the overall gameplay  potential can feel a bit limited  compared to the previous games creative  players will certainly make the best of  it though it's disappointing to see that  what you have at the beginning is  largely what you have by the end however  completing the game once will unlock the  original game plus mode replacing  Billy's original powers with blink  Domino and dark vision from dishonor to  bringing back old feelings from past  adventures in burials and Bank games is  the name from our cemeteries assignment  only taking seven hours to clear in the  normal setting  there are several locations that beg for  a return such as the mission to  infiltrate Karnataka's Bank leading to  one of the series most finely tuned  levels one feature brought in to add  more variety or the new contracts found  in the black market where you can also  buy items and upgrade your gear Billy  can take on a selection of side jobs  from the citizens in Kanaka ranging from  the bazaar such as killing an annoying  mime and making it look like an accident  to the more morbid like getting revenge  on a sadistic doctor who experiments on  his patients death of the outsider  channels much more of the spirit of  classic stealth action games giving room  to experiment and prod aspects of the  environment to see what works without  too many distractions from the story  along with a custom game mode allowing  you to tune enemy difficulty fail States  along with adding in a number of odd and  challenging options like Ironman mode  death of the outsider gives you a number  of ways to define the type of stealth  action game you want to play in a lot of  ways the more relaxed style does more to  complement the series is immersive sim  design compared to its predecessors kill  the outsider I trust you to finish this  I will doubt one way or another  dishonored death of the outsider is a  solid inventive yet somewhat subdued  capper to the stories from the previous  games while the smaller scope can be  felt throughout approach to allowing  players express themselves as a Master  Assassin is as strong as ever it's  uncertain where the series can go from  here but the standalone release proves  that dishonored is still a remarkably  designed at stealth action game with  much potential that offers players the  chance to be creative in ways they at  least expect  [Music]
 

